 "78": {
  "modified": "2026-10-30T07:34:02",
  "rendered": "<p><strong>Vientiane </strong><strong>Hash House Harriers VH3</strong></p>\n<p><strong>#2514</strong></p>\n<p>This Monday, the 2<sup>nd</sup> of November, A2B 5:30 departure from Ban Lao Beer Garden to Sticky Fingers, pay as you go. </p>\n<p>Happy Dancer is the Hare!</p>\n<p>Map to the run site:  <a href=\"https://goo.gl/maps/QcLCFDaSSiLbcCx56\">https://goo.gl/maps/QcLCFDaSSiLbcCx56</a></p>\n<p></p>"
 },
 "22": {
  "modified": "2026-11-05T03:31:22",
  "rendered": "<h1><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-family: Georgia;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Saturday  07 #,  November,  Hash-run no. 1569, hare is &#8220;NAKED&#8221;</span></span></span></strong></h1>\n<h3><strong>Start run at 4:30 pm., pay as you go </strong></h3>\n<h2 align=\"left\">Location: will be provided if the hash-site is decided </h2>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: Georgia;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">normal fee, </span></span><span style=\"font-family: Georgia;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">pay as u go </span></span></strong></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Falang: 70,000 Kip (80,000 Kip first timers) Lao: 30,000 Kip, Kids 2-12: 10,000 Kip 12- 18: 20.000kip, includes the beer in the circle, ice and water free, and cover the run with Joe Piss (200.000kip).</strong></span></h3>\n<h3><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>FUI:  VANG VIENG HASH EVENT end of NOVEMBER is from friday 27# 2 night end at the 29# sunday in Vang Vieng this year,  we are &#8220;planing&#8221; to go there with a bus for all participants who wont from the city directly to VV !  who like to join can &#8220;PRE-REGISTER&#8221; only at a normal saturday-Hash-Event (monday ore saturday) !!!! </strong></span></h3>\n<h3><strong>check our Whats-App website: &#8220;VBH3 hashlaos group&#8221;</strong></h3>\n<p>VBH3 was formed by six members of the VH3, who decided that they would like to have a weekend run in the countryside, rather than in the suburbs of Vientiane..</p>\n<p>The main difference from the VH3 is that there is only one run/walk and the &#8220;Circle&#8221; is held at the run site, mostly at a local Restaurant for food and drinks.</p>\n<p></p>"
 },
 "26": {
  "modified": "2026-11-05T03:33:01",
  "rendered": "<h2><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong> the month</strong>ly Bicycle-Hash November (no 199 ) is postponed !  / shifted to the o5# of December :       <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>the hare is  &#8220;SPUD&#8221;  </strong></span></span></h2>\n<h2><span style=\"color: #000000;\">we start at the JOMA Cafe` near the Nam Phu Fountain  <strong>at 9:30 am.</strong> with a STARTER offer from the Hare !!</span></h2>\n<h2><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong><strong style=\"color: #000080; font-size: 22px;\">check our  </strong></strong></span><span style=\"color: #0000ff;\"><strong>WhatsApp group: VBH3 hashlaos.com, </strong></span>our <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Messenger-App -group: &#8220;VTE Bike Riders&#8221;  and </strong></span><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>weekly bike-rides:  we meet every wednesday and friday at 7:45 am, at the Cafe` JOMA, depart at 8:00 am., everybody is very welcome &#8230;..</strong></span><strong>You have no Bike? Go out and rent one &#8230;..</strong></h2>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">“Bicycles, bicycles, I want to ride my bicycle. That seems to be a common theme these days”, thought Graeme “Mother Trucker” Bolger, a keen VH3 Monday and Bush Hasher. And so he formed the VH3 Monthly Bicycle Hash.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The inaugural Bike Hash Run # 1 was held on 30th May 2010 at Dongmakkhai, about 20 km north-east of Vientiane, with Mother Trucker as Hare. Since then the Bike Hash has been held on the last Sunday of every month, with a total of 80 rides completed by the end of 2016.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The number of participants on each ride now averages around 10 to 20, with a mixture of foreign residents, Lao nationals, members of other Hashes and visitors from all over the world.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The basic format of the VH3 Bike Hash is similar to that of the VH3 Bush Hash, with runs of 20-30 km in out-of-town areas, marked with lime, chalk and/or shredded paper. Generally, one or two ore 3 stops are made at a roadside shop or food stall for water (beer may also be on the menu) at the end we have a lunch in town.</p>"
 }
}